    {
      "source": "hackernews",
      "subsource": "news.ycombinator.com",
      "category": "ai",
      "title": "Stealing Reasoning Traces from Proprietary LLM APIs",
      "url": "https://stolen-thoughts.com/",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49257876",
      "score": 598,
      "comments": 271,
      "author": "quantumgarbage",
      "published": "2026-08-11T13:22:00Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Hidden Chain-of-Thought (CoT) reasoning traces in proprietary APIs can be extracted using specific prompt injection and side-channel techniques.",
        "Extracted traces facilitate low-cost model distillation, allowing attackers to replicate proprietary reasoning architectures without expensive baseline training.",
        "Providers must implement rigorous output sanitization and log monitoring to prevent unauthorized exposure of intermediate model reasoning steps."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
