      "author": "dayanruben",
      "published": "2026-08-11T16:59:09Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Modular released Mojo 1.0, combining Python's syntax with C-level performance using an MLIR-based compiler architecture.",
        "Implements Rust-like memory ownership, compile-time metaprogramming, and explicit hardware vectorization for low-level performance control.",
        "Provides seamless Python library interoperability, eliminating the two-language problem in production AI and machine learning pipelines."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "hackernews",
      "subsource": "news.ycombinator.com",
      "category": "security",
      "title": "Exploiting System Management Mode with a very long interrupt",
      "url": "https://github.com/xoreaxeaxeax/smiiiiiiiiiiiiiiii",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49245491",
      "score": 182,
      "comments": 77,
      "author": "WhiteDawn",
      "published": "2026-08-10T16:03:14Z",
      "bullets": [
        "SMI latency and extended interrupt handling expose race conditions inside x86 firmware before SMM context protection seals.",
        "Successful exploitation grants arbitrary execution in SMM (Ring -2), bypassing Secure Boot, OS kernel defenses, and hypervisor isolation.",
        "Firmware vendors must enforce strict hardware SMI locking, validate interrupt timing, and implement Intel/AMD firmware resilience checks."
      ]
    },
